From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: support the SM-T531 WCN3660 radio and native monitor

Consolidate the board WCNSS power domains/regulators, SMP2P/SMD wiring,
level-high DXE IRQs, valid PHY address, scan fallback and bounded transport
with native monitor RX/TX support. Keep all prior power and calibration
constraints; do not replace firmware or include device-specific secrets.

The stock API 1.5.1.2 / CRM12035159 image advertises scan offload but never
replies to channel-list request208. Select mac80211 software scan up front
for this exact RF/platform/image and retain generic fallback for others.
Clear stale software-scan state across stop/start and completion, and
propagate channel/scan errors instead of publishing a successful tune.

In exclusive monitor, use the tested stock HAL register ABI to bypass RXP
address/type filters and route unknown-key DPU frames to host RX. Keep
original register state for the monitor lifetime, verify writes and
restore it before normal operation. Preserve ciphertext/IV metadata and
validate raw TX headers/context. Reapply the filter after a successful
channel change without disabling RX on a rejected channel.

This patch contains the previously deployed Wi-Fi changes from patches
0013/0014/0015(WCNSS portion)/0031/0032/0123-0127 plus the lifecycle fixes.
See docs/WIFI.md for physical acceptance and firmware limitations. This
is not a claim of PMF/WPA3, arbitrary TX-rate controls or bad-FCS support.

Honor per-radio OF frequency limits with private band/channel copies. The
stock NV2 layout omits channel144 (vos_nvitem.c FEATURE_WLAN_CH144); the
installed firmware rejects it with status6. Describe that limit in the
board DT, without changing regulatory permissions on other channels.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>

---
